      "notes": "## 1. Guidance and results\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal found in the window. The Q3 2026 guidance was issued with Q2 results on 2026-08-06, before the window. It calls for \nrevenue up 7% to 11% QoQ, gross margin around 34%, and profit of 8.0 to 10.0 cents per diluted ADS\n — 2026-08-06 — https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/08/06/3339987/0/en/himax-technologies-inc-reports-second-quarter-2026-financial-results-provides-third-quarter-2026-guidance.html\n- \nPer MarketBeat, the EPS guide compared with a consensus of $0.09, and revenue guidance of $243.3M–$252.4M compared with a consensus of $238.7M\n — 2026-08-06 — https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/himax-technologies-nasdaqhimx-updates-q3-2026-earnings-guidance-2026-08-06/\n- Upcoming: \nHimax scheduled its Q3 2026 results call for Nov 5, 2026 at 8:00 AM EST\n — announced 2026-10-05 — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/HIMX/\n\n## 2. Analyst actions\n- \nWall Street Zen cut HIMX to \"Hold\"\n. The headline is dated Oct 24; the exact rating-change date isn't stated — approx. 2026-10-24 — https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NASDAQ/HIMX/\n- \nMarketBeat reported a three-analyst Hold consensus with an $8.00 target\n — 2026-10-24 — https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/boerse/news/corporate-news/robeco-adds-882-739-shares-himax-technologies-stock-sits-54-88-percent/70406339\n- Conflicting consensus figures: \nstockanalysis.com shows 3 analysts at \"Buy\" with a $30.2 target\n — date unknown — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/himx/\n- No named broker upgrades, downgrades, initiations or target changes were found in the window. The Morgan Stanley (Equalweight, target raised to $17.40) and Baird entries I found predate it — https://www.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/HIMAX-TECHNOLOGIES-INC-16677/consensus/\n- Danelfin, a quant model rather than a broker, \npublished a $12.27 three-month target\n — 2026-10-16 — https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/boerse/news/nebenwerte/danelfin-puts-a-usd-12-27-target-on-himax-technologies-stock/70348405\n\n## 3. Litigation and regulation\n- Nothing material found for Himax in the window: no lawsuits, investigations, fines or export-control actions. The Q2 release's risk factors still list \nchanges in export license regulated by EAR\n as a risk — 2026-08-06 — https://www.hongkongpressbulletin.com/article/932175651-himax-technologies-inc-reports-second-quarter-2026-financial-results-provides-third-quarter-2026-guidance\n\n## 4. Customer concentration\n- No new contract changes, losses or concentration disclosures found in the window.\n- Customer win: \nHimax announced that its WiseEye HX6538 AI processor was integrated into Alibaba's Qwen Glasses N1 series\n. \nThe release discloses no revenue, order volumes, pricing or guidance\n — 2026-10-14 — https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/10/14/3380540/8267/en/himax-wiseeye-ultralow-power-ai-adopted-in-alibaba-s-latest-qwen-glasses.html\n- The CEO referenced \nWiseEye's earlier adoption by a leading global technology company in its latest smart glasses\n. The customer isn't named — date unknown — same URL.\n\n## 5. Insider activity\n- CEO Jordan Wu's Form 4 reports \nvesting of 6,806 RSUs on Sept 30, 2026, giving 13,612 ordinary shares acquired\n. \nHis reported holdings afterward were 540,253 shares\n. This is an RSU settlement, not an open-market trade — 2026-09-30 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/HIMX/form-4-himax-technologies-inc-insider-trading-activity-1311c4a04f1d.html\n- A CFO Form 4 is listed as \nacquiring 3,916 shares, leaving 129,372 held directly\n. It was filed 2026-09-30, and the transaction date isn't shown in the snippet, so it is probably a vesting event — transaction date unconfirmed (filing 2026-09-30) — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/HIMX/\n- Context, outside the window: \na grant of 4,797 RSUs to the CEO on September 24, 2026\n — 2026-09-24 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/HIMX/form-4-himax-technologies-inc-insider-trading-activity-8fd926f2382d.html\n- No open-market insider sales, 10b5-1 sales or clustered selling found.\n- Institutional: \nRobeco Institutional Asset Management added 882,739 shares\n — 2026-10-23 — https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/boerse/news/corporate-news/robeco-adds-882-739-shares-himax-technologies-stock-sits-54-88-percent/70406339\n\n## 6. Product and competitive news\n- WiseEye HX6538: \nbuilt on Arm Cortex-M55 and Ethos-U55, running at 5 milliwatts\n — 2026-10-14 — https://www.streetinsider.com/news.php?id=27183288&classic=1\n- Other recent product items cited by Kalkine are \nan eDP touch-and-display driver for automotive displays on 8 September and a palm-vein authentication design in a smart lock on 18 August\n. Both predate the window — https://kalkine.com.au/news/technology/himax-nasdaqhimx-wins-alibaba-qwen-glasses-slot-for-its-wiseeye-ultralow-power-ai-chip\n- Co-packaged optics (CPO), company statement of 2026-08-06: \nGen 1 and Gen 2 products began engineering production ramps as scheduled in Q3\n. \nHimax says 2027 CPO shipments will significantly exceed 2026\n — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1342338/000117184326005288/exh_991.htm\n- Share price: \nHIMX closed at $11.94 on Oct 27, 2026\n. \nThat is down 17.3% over one month\n — 2026-10-27 — https://www.stocktitan.net/overview/HIMX/\n- No competitor, pricing or share-shift news found in the window.",
